From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:54:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give selected-plugin startup its fixture readiness deadline

The selected-plugin startup regression waits for an executor MCP process
using a generic two-second PID-file deadline. All six mention/discovery
variants fail at that deadline on native Intel Mac job 117157637027 while
the executor remains alive. The disconnect diagnostic follows teardown.

Expose a caller-supplied timeout in the test-only PID helper and use the
fixture's existing 20-second READ_TIMEOUT for these six startup cases.
Keep the two-second default for every existing caller. Preserve optional
startup grace, explicit-mention barriers, tool and analytics assertions.

Native diagnostic green: job 117180271287 passes all six original cases
in 51.32 seconds after an added 20-second readiness probe preceding the
original PID helper. Successful libtest capture hides individual probe
timings; the emitted helper change still requires final native acceptance.

Authoring green: maintained just fmt-check passes. Maintained Bazel app
server test command executes six cases on Linux: six passed, zero failed
or ignored, 1546 filtered, 4.30 seconds. Bazel reuses 6788 action results;
the filtered LONG-suite sizing advisory remains visible. Fresh queue and
full native CI remain required. Tracks codex-unleashed issue 61.
---
 .../tests/suite/v2/selected_capability_stack.rs          | 3 ++-
 codex-rs/core/tests/common/process.rs                    | 9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/selected_capability_stack.rs b/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/selected_capability_stack.rs
index 13c983ab9..7f6b93d6a 100644
--- a/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/selected_capability_stack.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/selected_capability_stack.rs
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ use codex_protocol::protocol::PLUGINS_INSTRUCTIONS_OPEN_TAG;
 use codex_utils_absolute_path::AbsolutePathBuf;
 use codex_utils_path_uri::PathUri;
 use core_test_support::process::wait_for_pid_file;
+use core_test_support::process::wait_for_pid_file_with_timeout;
 use core_test_support::responses;
 use core_test_support::responses::ResponsesRequest;
 use core_test_support::stdio_server_bin;
@@ -155,7 +156,7 @@ async fn selected_plugin_mcp_startup_respects_explicit_mentions(
     )
     .await??;
     let TurnStartResponse { turn } = to_response(response)?;
-    wait_for_pid_file(&fixture.pid_file).await?;
+    wait_for_pid_file_with_timeout(&fixture.pid_file, READ_TIMEOUT).await?;
     if explicitly_mentioned {
         // An explicit mention must outwait the optional one-second grace.
         tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(3)).await;
diff --git a/codex-rs/core/tests/common/process.rs b/codex-rs/core/tests/common/process.rs
index 82e42aac9..479944e80 100644
--- a/codex-rs/core/tests/common/process.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/core/tests/common/process.rs
@@ -4,7 +4,14 @@ use std::path::Path;
 use std::time::Duration;
 
 pub async fn wait_for_pid_file(path: &Path) -> anyhow::Result<String> {
-    let pid = tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2), async {
+    wait_for_pid_file_with_timeout(path, Duration::from_secs(2)).await
